Use cases
	Fixed device
		Config
			AP+HTTP
			Serial
			LCD
		Single AP saved
		Connect on boot
		While AP unavailable or connection failed
			Scan for available APs
			Display available APs
			Select AP
			Receive Password
			Connect
				On success Save Password

	Personal device, LCD config
		Background scanner
		While not connected
			If known/open WiFi exists AP
				Join preferred WiFi AP
			else
				Alert when unknown/open WiFi AP becomes available
		When WiFi requested
			Display available WiFi
			Select AP
			Receive password
			Connect
		When Manage WiFi requested
			Display saved WiFi APs
			Move up/down
			Delete

Configuration settings
	Number of Wifi AP credentials to save (0, 1, many)
	Use per-channel scan for background
	Scan Interval
	WiFi Authentication Mode (Console/LCD/AP)
		AP Name
	WiFi AP Preferences
		None
		Auto
		Manual

Tasks/Stores
	Saved WiFi Credentials List (of Preferred APs with credentials)
		Data
			Rank (implicit)
			Name
			Last Seen(?)
			Credential
			CredentialIsBad
		One of: Null, One, List
		Optional: Priority order
		Retrieve Credential for AP
		Save to NVRAM

	Available APs API
		Name
		Encryption/Auth
		Signal strength

	WiFi Connection manager
		Connect to saved AP:
			none saved: fail immediately
			only one saved: Attempt connection
			more than one saved:
				Scan available APs
				Order Available APs by Preferred AP rank, then by signal strength
				Match saved to available in order of priority
		On bad credentials:
			Mark saved credential as bad
		When no saved AP is available
			Background scan (end-user device), re-start when any good saved AP is available
		External indicator variables:
			Status: Scanning, Connecting, Connected, Failed (can't connect or no saved AP available)
			List of available APs open, unsaved, or wrong-credentialled

	WiFi Authentication UI
		Functions:
			Display Available APs (strength, encryption/auth, (un)credentialled, credential-bad, open)
			Select an AP
			Receive password
		Modes:
			LCD
			Console commands
				(Requires a Console to publish command availability)
			WiFi AP
				DNS
				DHCP
				HTTP

	WiFi AP Preferences UI
		GUI Screen to display, rank, delete preferred APs
